# UI stack and quality gates

## ShadCN + Tailwind

- Reuse primitives from `@/components/ui/*`; add new ones via the ShadCN CLI / `components.json`, not one-off copies.
- Style with Tailwind utilities and existing theme tokens in `src/index.css` (CSS variables). Avoid new CSS frameworks or inline style systems.
- Compose with `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` when merging classes.

## ESLint + typecheck + unit tests

- Match `frontend/eslint.config.js` (TypeScript + react-hooks). Do not disable rules to hide issues.
- Keep code type-safe: no unjustified `any`; prefer explicit Query/Mutation generics.
- Keep Vitest unit tests green (`npm test`); add or update co-located `*.test.ts(x)` when behavior changes.
- Pre-commit runs lint + typecheck when `frontend/` changes — fix failures instead of bypassing hooks.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — custom button + untyped fetch bypassing UI kit and typecheck
<button style={{ color: 'blue' }} onClick={() => fetch('/x')}>Save</button>

// ✅ GOOD — ShadCN + Tailwind tokens + typed handlers
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'

<Button type="button" variant="secondary" onClick={onSave}>
  Save
</Button>
```

From `frontend/`: `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm test`.
